  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `CLOB` contract implements a central limit order book (CLOB) for spot trading, supporting limit and fill orders, as well as order amendments and cancellations. The amendment logic is handled by the `amend()` function, which allows users to modify their existing orders' parameters, such as price, amount, and side, provided certain checks pass.\n\nA key restriction in the amendment logic is that only `POST_ONLY` orders can be amended (`amend()` enforces `if (args.limitOrderType != LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY) revert AmendNonPostOnlyInvalid();`). But if a `POST_ONLY` order has a price which would immediately fill the order (even partially) the function will revert with `PostOnlyOrderWouldFill()` via the `_executeBidLimitOrder()` or `_executeAskLimitOrder()` internal calls.\n\n**Summary of the flow:**\n- Users can only amend orders to be `POST_ONLY` orders.\n- If a user tries to amend an order to a price that would result in an immediate match (even partial), the transaction reverts.\n\n**Impact:**\n- Users are unable to amend their orders to a price where they would be filled, even if this is their intention (e.g., to cross the spread and take liquidity).\n- This restricts one of the main usages of amending an order, to move the order to the current price so it gets filled \n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nRemove the check if the order is a `POST_ONLY` function to allow the user to freely amend his order.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\nThe following coded POC shows that a user cannot amend an order to a price where it would be filled. The test attempts to amend a `POST_ONLY` order to a price that would cross the spread, expecting the transaction to revert with `PostOnlyOrderWouldFill()`.\n\nTo run the POC, replace the code in the file `test/c4-poc/PoC.t.sol` with the following code and run it with\n\n```solidity\nforge test -vv --mt test_can_not_amend_order_to_be_filled\n```\n\nFollowing is the terminal output of the POC:\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB} from \"../../contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {CLOB} from \"../../contracts/clob/CLOB.sol\";\nimport {Limit, MarketSettings} from \"../../contracts/clob/types/Book.sol\";\nimport {Order,Side} from \"../../contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\nimport {ICLOBManager, ConfigParams, SettingsParams} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOBManager.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"test/harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\nimport {console} from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n// ISSUE: can not amend an order pirce to it gets partialy filled\n        function test_can_not_amend_order_to_be_filled() external {\n            //set up\n            PoCTestBase.setUp();\n            address user1 = users[1];\n            address user2 = users[2];\n            //mint base tokens to user\n            baseToken.mint(user1, 100 ether);\n            quoteToken.mint(user2, 100 ether);\n\n            //start prank\n            vm.startPrank(user1);\n            //approve and deposit base tokens\n            baseToken.approve(address(accountManager), 100 ether);\n            accountManager.deposit(user1, address(baseToken), 10 ether);\n\n            //create postLimitOrderArgs for user (sell order)\n            ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args1 = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n                amountInBase: 1 ether,\n                clientOrderId: 0,\n                price: 1.5 ether,\n                cancelTimestamp: TOMORROW,\n                side: Side.SELL,\n                limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY\n            });\n\n            //post SELL order for user1\n            ICLOB.PostLimitOrderResult memory result = clob.postLimitOrder(user1, args1);\n            vm.stopPrank();\n\n            //get order ID\n            uint256 orderIdUser1 = result.orderId;\n\n            //start prank for user2\n            vm.startPrank(user2);\n            //approve and deposit quote tokens\n            quoteToken.approve(address(accountManager), 100 ether);\n            accountManager.deposit(user2, address(quoteToken), 10 ether);\n\n            //create postLimitOrderArgs for user2 (buy order)\n            ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args2 = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n                amountInBase: 1 ether,\n                clientOrderId: 0,\n                price: 1 ether,\n                cancelTimestamp: TOMORROW,\n                side: Side.BUY,\n                limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY\n            });\n\n            //post BUY order for user2\n            clob.postLimitOrder(user2, args2);\n            vm.stopPrank();\n\n         \n            // amend the SELL order of user1 to be partially filled by the BUY order of user2\n            ICLOB.AmendArgs memory amendArgs = ICLOB.AmendArgs({\n                orderId: orderIdUser1,\n                amountInBase: 2 ether,\n                price: 1 ether,\n                cancelTimestamp: TOMORROW,\n                side: Side.SELL,\n                limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY //i: \n            });\n\n            vm.startPrank(user1);\n            //expect revert\n            vm.expectRevert(CLOB.PostOnlyOrderWouldFill.selector);\n            //amend the order\n            clob.amend(user1, amendArgs);\n\n        }\n}\n```",
